IO-32: read grate type P_BAR-50x100 as P_BAR-50x100, not P_BAR-50

readGrateInletParams() looks the grate type up with findmatch(), which accepts
the first keyword that the token starts with. "P_BAR-50" comes before
"P_BAR-50x100" in GrateTypeWords and is a prefix of it, so P_BAR-50x100 was
always read as P_BAR-50, with that grate's splash-over velocity and open
area ratio. When findmatch() returns P_BAR-50, check for an exact
(case-insensitive) match of P_BAR-50x100.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-32_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..26cbea9 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -836,6 +836,10 @@ int readGrateInletParams(int i, char* tok[], int ntoks)
     grateType = findmatch(tok[4], GrateTypeWords);
     if (grateType < 0) return error_setInpError(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[4]);
 
+    // --- findmatch() stops at "P_BAR-50", a prefix of "P_BAR-50x100"
+    if (grateType == P50 && strcomp(tok[4], GrateTypeWords[P50x100]))
+        grateType = P50x100;
+
     // --- only read open area & splash velocity for GENERIC type grate
     if (grateType == GENERIC)
     {
